                     <handDesc>
                        
                        <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic">
                           <seg type="script">Eighteenth-century script.</seg>
                           <seg type="ink">Black, red, crimson.</seg>
                           <desc>Fine and careful.</desc>
                           <seg type="rubrication">Divine names; names of the donors; numbers and
                              titles of the Psalms; names of Hebrew letters in <ref cRef="betmas:LIT2000Mazmur.Ps118">Psalm 118</ref>; numbers and
                              titles of <ref target="#p1_i1.1"/>; the title and numbers of <ref target="#p1_i1.3"/>; 
                              doxology at the end of the parts of <ref target="#p1_i1.3"/>; five lines of the incipit of <ref target="#p1_i1.4"/>
                              alternating with two black lines; first two lines of the daily readings of
                              <ref target="#p1_i1.4"/>; some words and selected 3–4 lines of <ref target="#p1_i1.4"/>; introductory
                              prayer of <ref target="#p1_i1.5"/>; three lines of <ref target="#p1_i1.5"/> on <locus target="#158vb"/>; some words
                              of <ref target="#p1_i1.5"/>; elements of punctuation marks. The names of the owners and supplicants
                              on <locus target="#148rb"/> are rubricated in crimson.</seg>
                        </handNote>
                     </handDesc>
                     
                     <additions>
                        <list>
                           <item xml:id="a1">
                              <locus from="1r" to="1v"/>
                              <desc type="GuestText"><title type="incomplete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2797RepCh81">Malkǝʾ-hymn to Gabra Krǝstos</title>; very crudely written.</desc>
                              <q xml:lang="gez">ሰላም፡ ለከ፡ ሰላማዊ፡ መናኔ፡ ዓለም፡ ምድራዌ፡ አጽፈ፡ ድንግልና፡ ሥርግው፡</q>
                           </item>
                           
                           <item xml:id="a2">
                              <locus target="#1v"/>
                              <desc type="GuestText">Historiographical note at the bottom margin; approximately half is effaced. The note likely refers to the
                                 struggle between King <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS7102Minas">Minās</persName> (ʾAdmās Sagad) and his nephew <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS9358Tazkara">Tazkāra
                                    Dǝngǝl (Tazkāro)</persName> in <date>1560/61</date>. At the end, there is number <q xml:lang="gez">፶ወ፯</q>. It is carelessly written by a fine hand.</desc>
                              <q xml:lang="gez">አመ፡ ይጸብኡ፡ ምስለ፡ ሐፄ፡ አድማስ፡ ወተዝካሮ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis"/></q>
                           </item>
                           
                           <item xml:id="a3">
                              <locus target="#2r"/>
                              <desc type="OwnershipNote">Ownership note, crudely written by the same hand as <ref target="#a4"/> and <ref target="#a5"/>. The owner’s name is <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15060WaldaAbEgz">Walda ʿĀbiya ʾƎgzi</persName>; the name of his wife has been effaced.</desc>
                              <q xml:lang="gez">ዛቲ፡ መጽሐፍ፡ ዘወልደ፡ ዓቢየ፡ እግዚእ፡ ትኩኖ፡ መርሖ፡ ለመንግሥተ፡ ሰማያት፡ ወለብእሲቱ <gap reason="lost"/>.</q>
                              <q xml:lang="en">This is the book of Walda ʿĀbiya ʾƎgziʾ; may it be a guide to the Heavenly Kingdom for him and for his wife <gap reason="lost"/> .</q>
                           </item>
                           
                           <item xml:id="a4">
                              <locus target="#148r"/>
                              <desc type="OwnershipNote">Ownership note; crudely written by the same hand as <ref target="#a1"/> and <ref target="#a5"/>, the word <foreign xml:lang="gez">ማርያም</foreign> is rubricated. 
                                 It contains the names of the owners of the Psalter priest <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15061GabMar">Gabra Māryām</persName> and his wife <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15062WalMar">Walatta Māryām</persName>.</desc>
                              <q xml:lang="gez">ዝዳዊት፡ ዘቄስ፡ ገበረ፡ <hi rend="rubric">ማርያም፡</hi> ወብእሲቱ፡ ወለተ፡ <hi rend="rubric">ማርያም፡</hi></q>
                              <q xml:lang="en">This is a Psalter of priest Gabra Māryām and his wife Walatta Māryām.</q>
                           </item>
                           
                           <item xml:id="a5">
                              <locus target="#148r"/>
                              <desc type="GuestText"><title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT6946InvocationMary">Invocation to the Virgin Mary and Jesus Christ for
        protection</title>; the owner of the book and his family plead for Mary’s protection.
                                 At the end of the prayer the baptismal names of the owner <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15060WaldaAbEgz">Walda ʿĀbiya ʾƎgzi</persName> and members of his family are mentioned:
                                 <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15063GabKidan">Gabra Kidān</persName>, <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15064WaldaSel">Walda Śǝllāse</persName>, <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15062WalMar">Walatta Māryām</persName>, 
                                 <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15065TaklaGiyor">Takla Giyorgis</persName>, <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15066WalattaMuse">Walatta Muse</persName> and <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15067WalattaGior">Walatta Giyorgis</persName>. 
                                 The text is crudely written by the same hand as <ref target="#a1"/> and <ref target="#a4"/> ; the majority of the baptismal names are rubricated in crimson.
                              </desc>
                           </item>
                           
                           <item xml:id="a6">
                              <locus target="#158rb"/>
                              <desc type="OwnershipNote">Ownership note, containing the baptismal names of the owner and members of
                                 his family: <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15060WaldaAbEgz">Walda ʿĀbiya ʾƎgzi</persName>, <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15064WaldaSel">Walda Śǝllāse</persName>, <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15063GabKidan">Gabra Kidān</persName>, <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15061GabMar">Gabra Māryām</persName>.</desc>
                           </item>
                           
                           <item xml:id="a7">
                              <locus target="#162vb"/>
                              <desc type="Asmat">(above) ʾAsmāt-prayer; carefully written.</desc>
                              <q xml:lang="gez"/>ኢናዝልሞን፡ ኢናዝልሞን፡ ኢናዝልሞን፡ አሌክሙ፡ ሰላም፡ አሽኰር፡ አቁዶር፡ ወራፃ፡ ወነምር፡ ወናግ፡ ወደርከን፡ አለሞልም፡ ጥሪሲሆሙ፡ ወስነኒሆሙ፡ አዝማቹ፡ ሰአለ፡ በሕይወቱ፡ ወዘሞተ፡ በቦክቱ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="MK"/>
                           </item>
                           
                           <item xml:id="a8">
                              <locus target="#162vb"/>
                              <desc type="MagicText">(below) Magic recipe; very crudely written.</desc>
                              <q xml:lang="am"><gap unit="chars" quantity="3" reason="illegible"/>፡ የጐሽ፡ ሐር፡ የቁራ፡ ፀጉር፡ የብረት፡ ሐር፡ የሙጁ፡ ስር፡ ዶግ፡ ዝኵሉ፡ በማቅረጽ፡ በቅብ<gap reason="illegible"/> ቆቀባ፡</q>
                           </item>
                           
                           <item xml:id="a9">
                              <locus target="#163ra"/>
                              <desc type="GuestText"><title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT5678CommemorationRoch">Commemorative note and hymn for St Roch (Roqo)</title>; the text is identical to the one included in 
                                 <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/7M25BR4U"><seg type="book"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Synax2000SecondHalf"/><title level="m">&lt;hi rend="italics"&gt;መጽሐፈ ስንክሳር በግዕዝና በአማርኛ ከመጋቢት እስከ ጳጕሜን (&lt;/hi&gt;Mäṣḥafä sǝnkǝsar bägǝʿǝzǝnna bäʾamarǝñña kämäggabit ǝskä ṗagʷǝmen&lt;hi rend="italics"&gt;, ʻSynaxarion, in Geʿez, and in Amharic, from &lt;hi rend="italics"&gt;mäggabit&lt;/hi&gt; to &lt;hi rend="italics"&gt;ṗagumen&lt;/hi&gt; [second half of the year]ʼ)&lt;/hi&gt;</title><pubPlace>Addis Abäba</pubPlace><publisher>Tǝnśaʾe masattämiya dǝrǝǧǧǝt</publisher><date>2000</date><note type="tags"><note type="tag">bm:Synax2000SecondHalf</note></note><note type="tag">bm:Synax2000SecondHalf</note><citedRange unit="item">207</citedRange></bibl>. 
                                 Saint <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS12657Roch">Roch</persName> was given a covenant from Christ that those asking for his intercession
                                 will be spared from ‘pest’ (<foreign xml:lang="gez">ḥǝmāma bǝdbǝd</foreign>). The text is written in ink by a trained hand, the same as <ref target="#a10"/>.
                              </desc>
                              <q xml:lang="gez">እምገደለ፡ ቅዱስ፡ ሮቆ፡ ዝንቱስ፡ ቅዱስ፡ ኮነ፡ መስተጋድለ፡ እስከ፡ አርያም፡ ተአምረ፡ ወመንክረ፡ ወአሐተ፡ ዕለተ፡ ነደፎ፡ ሕማመ፡ ብድብድ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="MK"/></q>
                           </item>
                              
                              <item xml:id="a10">
                                 <locus target="#163rb"/>
                                 <desc type="Asmat">An ʾasmāt-prayer for an individual called <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15119WaldaSella">Walda Śǝllāse</persName> follows directly <ref target="#a9"/>. The supplicant asks for saving him
                                    from <foreign xml:lang="gez">bārya</foreign>, <foreign xml:lang="gez">ferā</foreign>, <foreign xml:lang="gez">nǝdād</foreign> (<locus target="#163rb11"/>) and <foreign xml:lang="gez">wabā</foreign> (<locus target="#163rb20"/>). 
                                    The text is written in ink by a trained hand, the same as <ref target="#a9"/>. 
                                    The last six lines of the text are blurred but still readable. In the upper margin, there are two captions, the one on the left being effaced.</desc>
                                 <q xml:lang="gez">በስመ፡ ሥሉስ፡ ቅዱስ፡ እስቶር፡ ስትሶር፡ ቶር፡ አላቶር፡ ሳቶሶር፡ እግቦ፡ ኦእግግቦ፡ ውግቦ፡ ውግግቦ፡ ግናር፡ ሳጦር፡ በ<gap unit="chars" quantity="1" reason="illegible"/>ጦርጦር፡ ዘወረደእምጽርሐ፡ ኢዮር፡ ወልደ፡
                                    እግዚአብሔር፡ ሕያው፡ በኃይለ፡ ዝንቱ፡ አስማት፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="MK"/></q>
                           </item>
                              
                           <item xml:id="a11">
                              <locus from="163v" to="164r"/>
                              <desc type="GuestText"><title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3038RepCh318">Hymn to St George</title>;  written in angular script by a practised hand. The last 3 lines of the text in <locus target="#163v"/> and the last 6 lines in <locus target="#164r"/>
                                 are effaced.</desc>
                              <q xml:lang="gez">አቄርብለከ፡ ስብሐት፡ ወጋዳ፡ ለጊዮርጊስ፡ ኮከበ፡ ልዳ። ሐሌሉያ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="MK"/></q>
                           </item>
                              
                           <item xml:id="e2">
                                 <locus target="#18r #39r #100v"/>
                                 <desc type="Correction">Corrections written over erased passages of text in <ref target="#h1">Hand 1</ref>.</desc> 
                              </item>
                              
                              <item xml:id="e3">
                                 <locus target="#35v #76r #127r #159va"/>
                                 <desc type="Correction">Corrections written over erased passages of text, in a secondary hand.</desc> 
                              </item>
                              
