                                 <desc>Writing exercises in fidal.</desc>
                              </item>
                              
                              <item xml:id="e6">
                                 <locus target="#16r #23v #34r #41v #77v #83v"/>
                                 <desc>The name <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15118NewayaMar">Nǝwāya Māryām</persName> is mentioned at the end of some Psalms.</desc> 
                              </item>
                              
                              <item xml:id="e7">
                                 <locus target="#113v #123r #129v #148r #148v #157v #162v #164v"/>
                                <desc>Writing exercises in pencil and pen.</desc> 
                              </item>
                              
                              <item xml:id="e8">
                                 <locus target="#140"/>
                                 <desc>Writing exercises in purple pen.</desc>
                              </item>
                              
                              <item xml:id="e9">
                                 <locus target="#153v #154r"/>
                                 <desc>Pen trials</desc>
                              </item>
                              
                           <item xml:id="e10">
                              <desc type="findingAid"><ref target="#p1_i1"/>,  <ref target="#p1_i1"/> and <ref target="#p1_i1"/> are divided into daily readings.
                                 The names of the weekdays were later crudely written, in a secondary hand, in the upper margin of the following folia:
                                 <locus target="#1v"/> <foreign xml:lang="gez">ዘሠኑይ</foreign>, <locus target="#23v"/> <foreign xml:lang="gez">ዘሰሉስ</foreign>,
                                 <locus target="#47v"/> <foreign xml:lang="gez">ዘረቡዕ</foreign>, <locus target="#68v"/> <foreign xml:lang="gez">ዘሐሙስ</foreign>,
                                 <locus target="#97r"/> <foreign xml:lang="gez">ዘአርብ</foreign>, <locus target="#113r"/> <foreign xml:lang="gez">ዘቅዳሜ</foreign>, 
                                 <locus target="#126v"/> <foreign xml:lang="gez">ዘእሑድ</foreign>.</desc>
                           </item>
                        </list>
                     </additions>
                     </physDesc>
                     <history>
                        <origin>
                           <origPlace>
                              <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0053SM">Sabayā Māryām</placeName>
                           </origPlace>
                           <origDate notBefore="1600" notAfter="1699" evidence="reign" cert="medium">Most likely 17th century.</origDate>  If the note in
                           <ref target="#a2"/> refers to King <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS7102Minas">Minās</persName> (ʾAdmās Sagad) and was written during his
                           reign, then the dating should be adjusted to the second half of the 16th century.                   
                        </origin>
                        <provenance>Priest <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15061GabMar">Gabra Māryām</persName> and his wife <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15062WalMar">Walatta Māryām</persName>
                           are mentioned as the owners in <ref target="#a4"/>. <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15060WaldaAbEgz">Walda ʿĀbiya ʾƎgzi</persName> is
                           mentioned as the owner in <ref target="#a3"/> and, together with <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15063GabKidan">Gabra Kidān</persName>, <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15064WaldaSel">Walda Śǝllāse</persName>, <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15062WalMar">Walatta Māryām</persName>, 
                           <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15065TaklaGiyor">Takla Giyorgis</persName>, <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15066WalattaMuse">Walatta Muse</persName> and <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15067WalattaGior">Walatta Giyorgis</persName> in a
                           prayer in <ref target="#a5"/>.</provenance>
                     </history>
                     
